# .graphifyignore — extra excludes for the Graphify knowledge graph.
# Complements Graphify's built-in _SKIP_DIRS (node_modules, build, dist, .git,
# .idea, target, out, graphify-out, .worktrees, ... are already skipped).
# Keep this list to genuinely heavy / generated / duplicate / non-architectural
# paths so the graph stays a clean map of the SOURCE, not of caches or copies.

# Gradle / Kotlin daemon caches (large, no architectural signal)
.gradle/
.kotlin/

# Sibling repo checkouts used by other tooling (full duplicates of the tree)
.codex-security-worktrees/

# Stray compiled / decompiled artifacts committed at the repo root
*.class
RecoverProfileScreen*.java

# Local backup copies created by tooling (avoid duplicate doc processing)
*.bak-*

# ── Prose authorities excluded from the STRUCTURAL graph (ADR-MEM-001) ────────
# Graphify indexes CODE / tests / build / schemas. Product, science, decisions,
# governance and audit PROSE belong to the Markdown canon (Obsidian view), not the
# code graph — they currently pollute it as fake communities (e.g. the CLAUDE.md
# "Aprendizajes acumulados" section became a graph community hub).
# Takes effect on the NEXT `graphify update .` (deferred until the tree is clean).
# PRESERVED on purpose (deliberately NOT excluded): docs/knowledge/** — the curated
# cognitive-science corpus is an intentional ingestion (memory: project_cognitive-science-corpus).
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
MINDBOOST_AUDIT_LEDGER.md
docs/context-pack/
docs/context_pack/
docs/memory/
docs/audits/
docs/architecture/
docs/mindboost_velocidad_implementation_plan/
docs/mindboost_scoring/
docs/mindboost_profile_v2/
